president john f kennedy's all-too-brief  life was documented like none before in  photos that helped build the image of a  young leader with more than a touch of  glamour this year to mark the 100th  anniversary of his birth many of these  images are being shown in an exhibition  now touring the country which just  opened here in New York and not what  your country can do for you ask what you  can do for your country  john f kennedy's 1961 inauguration  address remains one of the most  memorable moments in American history  shortly before those historic remarks  Kennedy and his wife Jackie were all  smiles as they made their way from the  snowy White House to the Capitol this  picture is part of a new exhibit at the  New York Historical Society Museum  showing Kennedy's public and private  moments what you see in this exhibit is  not JFK as a politician not JFK winning  an election or making a point in  Congress or giving a speech but you see  him as a father Yunus grandmother my  mother  Stephen Kennedy Smith jr. is a cousin of  the 35th president and co-author of JFK  a vision for America which includes  everything from drafts of speeches to  over 500 photographs of Kennedy we went  through 34,000 photos from America's  greatest documentary photographers and  put them together into the book and the  exhibit some of the photographs reveal  the weight of Kennedy's public life like  this one of a pained president hunched  over the Oval Office desk while others  show quieter moments like this 1958  photo showing Kennedy beside his infant  daughter Caroline or this snapshot from  the 1960 presidential campaign showing a  group of young admirers looking on as  Kennedy worked on a speech it also  covers the devastation following  Kennedy's assassination capturing a  glimpse of Jackie on the day of her  husband's state funeral a hope is that  visitors will come away with new insight  into one of the most captivating  presidents in history I want them to be  intrigued I want them to be inspired I  want them to be curious and I want them  to read  Kennedy's words and that's really the  whole point of this project the exhibit  opened yesterday in New York it's also  running at the Smithsonian Art Museum  until September 7th here through January  7th and if people want to learn more  about it we have on our CBS this morning  Instagram page sort of taking you  through the life of JFK some amazing  pictures though that I had not seen  before  yeah it's interesting I think he was the  first president who is really  photographed as in you know as intensely  as as this it's just incredible  documents you feel like you were there  and living some of those moments
 

